---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { site } from "../../data/site";

// The "Delete data URL" entered in Play Console's Data safety form for our
// Google Play apps. Our data sits in the game's own one small Firebase
// database — leaderboard runs and bug reports — so deletion happens in the
// game (ERASE MY RUNS) or by request to us. Companion to /privacy/apps,
// which is the full policy.
const contact = "sheibeck@gmail.com";
const subject = encodeURIComponent("Delete my Delve, Die, Repeat leaderboard runs");
const bugSubject = encodeURIComponent("Delete my Delve, Die, Repeat bug report");
---
<Layout
  title="Delete your data — Google Play apps"
  description="How to delete the leaderboard runs or bug report Darktier Studios apps on Google Play have sent to our one small Firebase database, or request that we delete them for you."
>
  <div class="container">
    <section style="padding:84px 0 28px">
      <p class="kicker">Darktier Studios · legal · Google Play apps</p>
      <h1 style="font-size:clamp(40px,6vw,72px);line-height:1.04;letter-spacing:-0.02em;margin:0 0 0 -0.06em">Delete your data</h1>
      <p class="privacy-meta">Applies to <strong>Delve, Die, Repeat</strong> (<code>com.darktierstudios.delvedierepeat</code>) · {site.legalName}</p>
    </section>

    <article class="privacy">
      <p class="privacy-lede">
        We keep one small database on Google Firebase for two things: your <strong>leaderboard runs</strong>
        and the <strong>Google Play Games name</strong> shown beside them, both sent only while the in-game
        <strong>Compete</strong> setting is on, and a <strong>bug report</strong> you chose to send. Delete
        either one yourself in about a minute, right from the game.
      </p>

      <h2>Delete your leaderboard data</h2>
      <ol>
        <li>In the game, open the account block — the ☰ menu in the dungeon, or the corner chip on the
          title screen.</li>
        <li>Tap <strong>ERASE MY RUNS</strong>.</li>
        <li>Tap it again to confirm.</li>
      </ol>
      <p>
        That deletes every run of yours on the leaderboard, in every season, the board name we recorded for
        you, and your game account together with its Google Play Games link. Your local run history (YOUR
        DEAD) stays on your phone. A later run you send, after signing in again, starts a new game account
        under your Google Play Games name.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Google's side:</strong> to disconnect the game from your Google Play Games account, use the
        game's entry in Google Play Games settings. You can also delete your Play Games account and its
        data in your Play Games profile or Google MyAccount; that is Google's data, which we cannot delete
        for you.
      </p>

      <h2>Stop sending new data</h2>
      <p>
        In the same account block, set <strong>COMPETE</strong> to <strong>OFF</strong>. With Compete off,
        nothing is sent and you are not signed in to Google Play Games, any runs still waiting to be sent
        are thrown away, runs you finish from then on are never uploaded later — even if you turn Compete
        back on — and the game stays fully playable.
      </p>

      <h2 id="bug-reports">Delete a bug report</h2>
      <p>
        A report sent from <strong>REPORT A BUG</strong> in the game's ☰ menu carries no account, email
        address, or other contact detail. It is stored in the game's Google Firebase project and posted
        publicly as an issue on the game's GitHub repository
        (<a href="https://github.com/sheibeck/ddr" target="_blank" rel="noopener">github.com/sheibeck/ddr</a>).
        A small limit record behind the cooldown and daily cap on reports is deleted automatically about 2
        days after your last report. To have a report itself deleted, email
        <a href={`mailto:${contact}?subject=${bugSubject}`}>{contact}</a> with the link to its GitHub
        issue, or roughly when you sent it and what it said. We will delete it from Firebase and GitHub and
        confirm when it's done.
      </p>

      <h2>Everything else is already yours</h2>
      <p>
        Your current run, local run history, personal bests, and settings live only on your device.
        Uninstalling the app deletes them. We keep one small database on Google Firebase for the public
        leaderboard and bug reports, nothing else — so apart from runs you sent to the leaderboard, the
        board name beside them, and a bug report you chose to send, there is nothing further for us to
        erase.
      </p>

      <h2>Need help?</h2>
      <p>
        If you can't use ERASE MY RUNS — for example, you've already uninstalled the game — email
        <a href={`mailto:${contact}?subject=${subject}`}>{contact}</a> with your Google Play Games name,
        and roughly when you last played, and we'll delete your leaderboard runs and board name and confirm
        when it's done.
      </p>

      <p>
        Full policy: <a href="/privacy/apps">privacy policy for our apps</a>.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</Layout>
